I'm sorry, I cannot really figure out what are you asking about. You may be mixing two different APIs.

org.rosuda.JRI.Rengine is the low-level API and you can certainly use re.assign("x", "y") yo have the same effect as
x <- "y"
in R.

On the other hand REngineException is a class from another API in org.rosuda.REngine which is a high-level API that can work with different back-ends like JRI or Rserve and is raised when using org.rosuda.REngine.REngine sub class.

So please clarify which API you use, what are you trying to do and what problem are you facing. If you have errors you are dealing with, please copy/paste them in verbatim as well as the complete code.

Cheers,
Simon

