From urbanek at research.att.com  Mon Feb 17 16:16:02 2014
From: urbanek at research.att.com (Simon Urbanek)
Date: Mon, 17 Feb 2014 11:16:02 -0500
Subject: Mac OS X 10.9 Mavericks - JGR and Java tips
Message-ID: <B9343F4F-1C4B-4DBA-BF69-285F8974BD32@research.att.com>

Note that Mac OS X 10.9 upgrade creates a bit of a Java mess. If you try to use Java it may be removed by the installer and crashes with CRAN binaries. Easiest to see is if you start JGR and it just crashes - then you don't have the right Java installed. Unfortunately Apple's JAva updates doesn't work if not run from their java command.

The trick is to get Apple's Java 1.6 - probably the easiest is to go to Terminal and type

R CMD javareconf -n

which tries to configure Java for R and should trigger a prompt where the OS is asking if you want to install Java 1.6 and you say yes. Once it downloads Java you can try to re-runt he above and it should succeed. (Possibly just typing "java" may also do the trick, but checking it with R is a good idea).

Cheers,
Simon

